{"title":"2017 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The smallest positive integer greater than 1 that leaves a remainder of 1 when divided by 4, 5, and 6 lies between which of the following pairs of numbers?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e343089e59a334f05a2224e497f127b8e57e03c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }2\\text{ and }19\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }20\\text{ and }39\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }40\\text{ and }59\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }60\\text{ and }79\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }80\\text{ and }124$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"678\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the remainder is the same for all numbers, then we will only need to find the lowest common multiple of the three given numbers, and add the given remainder.The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c936a08d585ccf7bfc6bb008ddce6f48ce17adfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{LCM}(4,5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed173b4b6854cee9ba8a5ab834d47933dd506727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+1=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />, that is in the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397f0cef03ed882525f69ea647c41335fcaeb4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{60 and 79}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the number we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We can say that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/3/253b4a316681500502a2cfca6ee6ba8005a8dc02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 1 \\mod 4\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd82797818d62bf375e80ff0a90a2c61d8a51f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 1 \\mod 5\\]\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d89f62bc17793757f37ac1a06d81cafce7ea80e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n \\equiv 1 \\mod 6.\\]\" width=\"115\" height=\"12\" />\nWe can also say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1eeda6c7d64cf8688e3ee0b3324d5559b4ad6008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4,5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/e/1de3ed5fb7fa9b1fa73395d65c43e5bc81cd9d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" />\nTherefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/0/460bdfc9ac3f0ea4b8a84046e2387b17d37a2bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1=lcm(4,5,6)=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf55651a72396aeb96bee1fe17474cf6d3a365d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=60+1=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"129\" height=\"15\" /> which is in the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397f0cef03ed882525f69ea647c41335fcaeb4af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{60 and 79}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"121\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~PEKKA\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING!!!)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UIrHmHT_jl4\">https://youtu.be/UIrHmHT_jl4</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/SwgXyYFIuxM\">https://youtu.be/SwgXyYFIuxM</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kNIx_iDhVD4\">https://youtu.be/kNIx_iDhVD4</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nOSqQjEv0U0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nOSqQjEv0U0</a>   ~davidxxxx\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; bo